# double_spaced_verse.txt — the verse lines, by construction.
#
# The file is one line of text, one blank line, throughout: the shape a PDF
# text layer produces when it renders leading as whitespace. Between the two
# Donne stanzas the gap is two blanks, which is the boundary the extraction
# leaves for a real stanza break.
#
# One range, not two. A stanza gap belongs inside a protected passage — see
# the block-extension note in protect.py — so the two stanzas of one poem are
# a single span, and the blanks between them are inside it.
#
# Derived from the text of the fixture, not from running the detector over it.

20-55
